    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Offers in excess of €359,000\r\n\r\n'Spacious A2-Rated Three-Bedroom Home in a Highly Convenient Wexford Location'\r\n\r\nKehoe & Assoc. are delighted to present No. 28 Meadow Avenue, Whitebrook to the market, an impressive three-bedroom, three-bathroom mid-terrace residence extending to c. 122 sq.m. Offering generous, well-proportioned accommodation over two floors, this modern A2-rated home combines excellent energy efficiency with comfortable contemporary living.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation is thoughtfully arranged and begins with a welcoming entrance hallway and guest w.c. The sitting room provides a comfortable separate living space, while the kitchen offers excellent proportions for everyday family life and entertaining. A practical utility room is plumbed with space for a washing machine, providing valuable additional functionality with a separate sink and ample storage. \r\n\r\nUpstairs, there are three bedrooms, all of which benefit from fitted slide robes. The main bedroom is further enhanced by its own private en-suite, while a family bathroom serves the remaining bedrooms. With three bathrooms in total and an overall floor area of approximately 122 sq.m., No. 28 offers an excellent sense of space throughout.\r\n\r\nExternally, the property benefits from an enclosed west-facing rear garden, ideally positioned to capture the afternoon and evening sunshine. This garden and sunny orientation provides an attractive outdoor extension to the living accommodation and an ideal setting for summer dining, entertaining or simply relaxing at the end of the day.\r\n\r\nWhitebrook enjoys an excellent position on the outskirts of Wexford Town, combining the convenience of town living with easy access to an impressive range of sporting, recreational and coastal amenities. Wexford Golf Club is close by, while Wexford Town Centre offers an extensive selection of shops, supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, schools and everyday services. The location also provides convenient access to the N25 and wider national road network. \r\n\r\nFor those who enjoy the outdoors, some of County Wexford’s best-known coastline is within comfortable driving distance, including Curracloe Beach and Rosslare Beach, making this an excellent base from which to enjoy Wexford’s renowned coastal lifestyle. Both Curracloe and Rosslare Strand are approximately 20 minutes’ drive from this general area of Wexford Town.\r\n\r\nThe property is also well positioned for commuters. Wexford (O Hanrahan) at Redmond Square provides rail connections on the Dublin–Rosslare line, while regular bus services provide further connections to Dublin and beyond.\r\n\r\nCombining 122 sq.m. of spacious accommodation, an A2 energy rating, three bedrooms, three bathrooms and a west-facing garden, No. 28 Meadow Avenue represents an attractive opportunity for first-time buyers, families or those seeking a modern, energy-efficient home within easy reach of Wexford Town and the coast.\r\n\r\nIt is highly recommended, to arrange a suitable viewing time, please contact the sole selling agents, Kehoe & Assoc., at 053 9144393."
      },
